{"text":"We cover loss or damage caused by water escaping from fixed water or heating systems, including pipes, tanks, radiators, cylinders, taps, toilets, showers, washing machines and dishwashers, as well as water leaking from underground supply or drainage pipes that serve the home. This includes damage to the buildings and, if shown on your schedule, your contents. We may also cover the cost of finding the source of the leak and making good any damage that is necessary to reach it, up to the limits shown in your policy.

We do not cover wear and tear, gradual seepage, poor workmanship, corrosion, lack of maintenance, or damage caused by water entering the home from outside. We also do not cover loss caused by a leak you knew about and did not deal with promptly. If the home has been left unoccupied for more than 30 days, different conditions may apply, and you must take reasonable steps to protect it from frost and burst pipes.

You must turn off the water supply, where possible, and tell us as soon as you can after discovering a leak."}
